      "writtenOn": "2023-03-22T18:09:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t know what the right contract here is so just opening for discussion, but like insert recording on the queueManager can fail for multiple reason before we ever call Recording::addCommands. In all those cases we call the finishedProc that was passed into insert recording. So if the finished procs stored on the recording are meant to be purely the same then I think they should be called as well (maybe pull them off the recording early and just pass the array of finished procs combined with passed in one around as a unit).\n\nBut at the same time I can see arguments for the finishedProc on the recording to be a little special and more tied to the recording itself. So maybe they shouldn\u0027t be called for other failures?\n\nIf I had to pick I think I\u0027d lean towards first option, but don\u0027t have a strong opinion either way.",
      "parentUuid": "49a342e3_426b1c1d",
      "range": {
